# The CDN assets the *docs pages* load, pinned by content rather than just by version.
#
# One source of truth for two jobs:
#   1. the `integrity="sha384-…"` attributes web/docsbase.html renders, and
#   2. `make vendor`, which refuses to write a file whose digest doesn't match — used to
#      preview or measure the pages with no egress (`rendocs -base /vendor`).
#
# Only the design system is here, and only because the guide has no build step: it is four
# static HTML files on GitHub Pages, so its dependencies have to arrive from somewhere at
# runtime, and a pinned jsDelivr URL with an integrity attribute is the honest way to do
# that. The *app* has no entry here at all — Vue, marked, DOMPurify and mermaid are npm
# dependencies of web/ui, bundled by Vite into web/dist and served from the binary, so
# their versions live in web/ui/package.json and their bytes in web/ui/package-lock.json.
#
# Every path is <package>@<version>/<path-inside-the-npm-tarball> — the same shape jsDelivr
# and unpkg serve. Digests are of the published npm bytes.
#
# To upgrade: change the version here, run `make vendor` to fetch it, and copy the digest
# it reports in. AGENTS.md quotes this version too, and a test fails when they disagree.

8bit-nes@0.7.2/all.min.css                sha384-HeVMkfD21Nr0RP7CR6MHr8eGuaVXvD3OtLKN5Da5MN4OXox3euzDqTBkEFyx7Osl
